# ── Build artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# _dist/ — PAC CLI solution zip staging (Tables, Flows, Env Vars starters)
_dist/
# dist/  — Vite/SPA build output (Power Apps, Power Pages starters)
#
# NOTE — this pattern is UNANCHORED, so it matches a dist/ directory at ANY depth. That is
# intended for build output, but it is a trap for vendored packages: @smkbacil/design-ui ships
# all of its code inside dist/, so committing an UNPACKED copy under vendor/ would commit only
# package.json + README.md and silently drop every build artifact -- `git add` reports nothing,
# CI installs a shell package, and the build dies later on missing exports.
# That is one of the reasons the vendored package is a .tgz (not ignored) rather than a folder.
# See scripts/vendor-design-ui.ps1.
dist/
*.zip

# ── Node.js ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Environment / secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
# ...but the SHIPPED templates must reach every clone. Without these negations the Code Site's
# .env.example (the VITE_PORTAL_URL template) was gitignored, so no clone ever received it.
!.env.example
!.env.template
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ── Log files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── PAC CLI / Power Platform exports ──────────────────────────────────────────
_temp_*/

# ── Claude Code ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# settings.json is committed (team-wide allowlist) — settings.local.json is not
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Editor / IDE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.cursor/
.fleet/
*.code-workspace
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# ── OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ── Power Pages Code Site ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-developer / per-environment manifest — regenerated by pac, not shared
**/.portalconfig/*-manifest.yml
# Live-site download snapshot — local reference only
**/powerpages-live-check/

# ── Cloud Flows / PAC ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Filled-in per-environment deploy settings (deployment-settings-template.json IS committed)
deployment-settings.json
# PAC solution unpack output
*_unpacked/

# ── Local state / scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# guid-freshen marker (Tables + Code Site) - prevents an accidental second run.
# COMMITTED on purpose. It records a fact about the SOLUTION ("fresh GUIDs are live in
# Dataverse"), not about one developer's machine, and apply-config.ps1 -> Test-PrefixGuard
# reads it as a hard gate on re-mapping shortPrefix. While it was ignored, that gate was
# inert on every clone except the one where the freshen happened to run - so a second
# developer could re-map the prefix and silently break the deployed forms and views.
# Both writers keep the content machine-independent for exactly this reason.
!**/.guid-freshened
# Scratch notes
**/SECURITY-TODO.md
